{"text":"Hugh: coordinate and complete the inventory application adoption in the gitseq-inventory repository, using the released Tailapps jsonataddl module and that repository’s own workroom and target ref.","body":{"conditions":"This replaces the pre-design Gitseq-local implementation request 218a6a1d, whose target and scope conflict with the adopted repository split in notes/2026-09-04-tailapps-jsonataddl-adoption.md. Begin only after the Tailapps release coordination request 79460d1d is satisfied with an immutable public module tag. In gitseq-inventory, file and carry the design’s I2, I3, I4, and I8 work through its own durable requests: define GitseqRecord and the three host identity components; build the four thin host adapters, transaction boundary, projection identity and reuse rules; land the three corpora including input-contract freeze and planted-defect proof; then rewrite and bind the inventory application to the exact tagged github.com/generalbusiness-ai/tailapps/jsonataddl module. Preserve the design’s pins, deterministic replay, default-deny authority, logical-value boundary, public module license/provenance, and all go/no-go gates. Use the gitseq-inventory repository’s intended target ref, which need not be main, and merge only exact independently approved heads under that workroom’s discipline; push, verify CI, and clean each worktree/branch. Do not change Gitseq source under this coordination request. Report here the exact external requests, reviewed landing receipts, target refs and heads, module version/checksum, composed runtime digest, corpus evidence, and CI results. This coordination request owes no Gitseq artifact and closes only by explicit report and planner ratification after that external evidence is verified.","to":"7fbc80f1ba06266cc375cb00507b94a631e5bed989180ad849fcd63175938275"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:218a6a1de664b7954717760b0af40b4460bc0c4b","retirement":"git:sha1:5d26227